  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/esa-work-meaning
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: A required WRA work placement is expressly separated from the chapter-41 work provisions; no equivalence is inferred.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol9-ch53/0016
      quote: "53072 Where a claimant is required to undertake a work placement as part of their WRA action plan, this\n\nis not paid or unpaid work. The guidance in DMG Chapter 41 about work 1, including exempt work2 and\n\nremunerative work3, does not apply.\n\n\n                                                               1 ESA Regs, reg 40 & 44; 2 reg 45; 3 reg 41"
      locator: DMG 53072
  - target: term/esa-limited-capability-work-related-activity
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The source says the WRA requirement ceases on support-group membership, which is associated with LCWRA in the capability chapter.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol9-ch53/0017
      quote: "53080 The requirement to undertake WRA ceases to have effect if the claimant becomes a member of\n\nthe support group1. See DMG 53011 for the meaning of “member of the support group”.\n\n\n                                                          1 ESA (WRA) Regs, reg 3(3); WR Act 07, s 24(4)"
      locator: DMG 53080
    - page: page/dmg-vol8-ch42/0081
      quote: "42612 Claimants with the most severe illnesses or disabilities who have LCWRA will receive the support\n\ncomponent1 without conditionality although they may participate in work-related activity on a voluntary\nbasis if they so wish.\n\n\n                                                                               1 WR Act 07, s 2(2) & 4(4)"
      locator: DMG 42612
